<title>INDIA: Indian soybean prices climb, oil and solvent slip.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean prices climb, oil and solvent slip.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices rose by 100-150 rupees per tonne on Wednesday, dealers said.</p>
<p>Arrivals were around 10,000 tonne in central Indian markets on Wednesday, they said. Soyoil prices remained weak on heavy selling pressure and limited demand. Soyoil solvent was down by 100 rupees per tonne and soyoil refined was steady.</p>
<p>Exports demand was at a low level. Soymeal yellow was $271 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was $135-136 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was 4,650 rupees FOR Bedibunder and was 4,600-4,625 rupees FOR Bhavnagar.</p>
